~proposed~~`\nL148: \nL149: `editing`\nL150: 【22†#9】 by 【23†Robert C. Lyons】 at Sun Apr 26 13:15:30 EDT 2026\nL151: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA395495 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A395495)\nciteturn4view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn0view0\",\"lineno\":27}); Total lines: 142\nL0: 【0†login】\nL1: \nL2: The OEIS is supported by 【1†the many generous donors to the OEIS Foundation†oeisf.org】.\nL3: \nL4: 【2†Winners in the A400K Celebration】\nL5: \nL6: [Input]\nL7: \nL8: [Input]\nL9: \nL10: 【3†Hints】\nL11: \nL12: (Greetings from 【4†The On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences】!)\nL13: \nL14: A395495\nL15: \nL16: Minimum number of cells in a connected polyomino on the square grid that contains every fixed n-omino as a translated subregion.\nL17: \nL18: 1\nL19: \nL20: 1, 3, 5, 9, 13, 18, 24, 31, 39\nL21: \nL22: (【5†list】; 【6†graph】; 【7†refs】; 【8†listen】; 【9†history】; 【10†text】; 【11†internal format】)\nL23: \nL24: OFFSET\nL25: 1,2\nL26: \nL27: COMMENTS\nL28: \nL29: Containment is translation-only: the contained piece may not be rotated or reflected. Number of fixed n-ominoes is 【12†A001168】. Each of a(1) through a(9) is proved via SAT + CEGAR connectivity and carries a DRAT UNSAT certificate at k = a(n) - 1 that is independently verified by drat-trim. A pure-Python geometric containment verifier also re-confirms that every reported container does contain every fixed n-omino as a translate.\nL30: Conjecture: a(n) = (n^2 - n + 6)/2 for n >= 4, with a(n) = 2n - 1 for n in {1, 2, 3}. Equivalently a(n) = 【13†A000217】(n-1) + 3 for n >= 4. Predicts a(10) = 48.\nL31: At n = 7 every minimum container has a single 1-cell interior hole. SAT model-enumeration over the 7 X 7 bounding box (the natural search box, which must contain both the horizontal and vertical n-cell I-omino) finds exactly four 24-cell containers; all four are the 25-cell discrete L_1 ball of radius 3 (centered in the 7 X 7 box) minus one cell from the D_4 orbit at L_1 distance 2 from the center, and all contain a hole. A wider 8 X 8 search at k = 23 returns UNSAT (LRAT certified).\nL32: The hole is therefore a structural feature of a(7), distinguishing this sequence geometrically from the purely numerical match 【14†A350660】. For n in {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9} the optimal container is simply connected.\nL33: LINKS\nL34: \nL35: 【15†Table of n, a(n) for n=1..9.】\nL36: \nL37: Peter Exley, 【16†Solver code, data, and figures†github.com】, GitHub.\nL38: \nL39: EXAMPLE\nL40: \nL41: Optimal containers, with one example per illustrated n. Cells are marked '#'; empty cells are '.'.\nL42: \nL43: The 1 container with bounding box 3 X 3:\nL44: \nL45: . # .\nL46: # # #\nL47: \nL48: . # .\nL49: \nL50: .\nL51: \nL52: The 1 container with bounding box 4 X 4:\nL53: \nL54: . . # .\nL55: \nL56: . # # .\nL57: \nL58: # # # #\nL59: \nL60: . # # .\nL61: \nL62: .\nL63: \nL64: The 1 container with bounding box 5 X 5:\nL65: \nL66: . . # . .\nL67: \nL68: . # # # .\nL69: \nL70: # # # # #\nL71: \nL72: . # # # .\nL73: \nL74: . . # . .\nL75: \nL76: .\nL77: \nL78: One of 4 D_4-equivalent containers with bounding box 7 X 7 (the single dot at row 3 column 3 is the interior hole):\nL79: \nL80: . . . # . . .\nL81: \nL82: . . # # # . .\nL83: \nL84: . # . # # # .\nL85: # # # # # # #\nL86: \nL87: . # # # # # .\nL88: \nL89: . . # # # . .\nL90: \nL91: . . . # . . .\nL92: \nL93: .\nL94: \nL95: The 1 container with bounding box 9 X 9:\nL96: \nL97: . . . . . # . . .\nL98: \nL99: . . . . # # . . .\nL100: \nL101: . . . # # # . . .\nL102: \nL103: . . # # # # # # #\nL104: \nL105: . # # # # # # # #\nL106: # # # # # # # # #\nL107: \nL108: . . . # # # . . .\nL109: \nL110: . . . # # # . . .\nL111: \nL112: . . . # # # . . .\nL113: \nL114: CROSSREFS\nL115: \nL116: Cf. 【17†A327094】 (the free-piece analog), 【12†A001168】 (number of fixed n-ominoes (the family contained)), 【18†A000105】 (number of free n-ominoes), 【13†A000217】.\